From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <noreply@xe.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:30:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/50] experiment: direct guest-to-texture route for <controlledframe> (no capture device)

controlledframe.createTextureSource({width, height, maxFrameRate, poolSize})
returns a GuestFrameTextureSource whose read() resolves with a VideoFrame
backed by an RGBA shared image that the display compositor filled with the
guest's pixels (CopyOutputRequest + BlitRequest into a renderer-owned shared
image; no readback, no media capture device, no format conversion).

- blink.mojom.GuestFrameTextureHost (per frame, DocumentService in content):
  CopyGuestFrame(RemoteFrameToken, ExportedSharedImage, SyncToken, size,
  wait_for_new_frame). Only accepts the proxy of an inner (guest)
  WebContents' main frame whose outer delegate frame is a child of the
  calling frame; fenced frames and ordinary iframes are refused.
- viz: CopyOutputRequest::wait_for_new_frame(); CompositorFrameSinkSupport
  holds such requests until a frame newer than the last one copied for a
  waiting request activates (damage-driven, one copy per new guest frame).
- Blink: GuestFrameTextureSource ([IsolatedContext], webcodecs module) with
  a ring of renderer-allocated shared images, rate cap, release sync tokens.
- controlled frame bindings: createTextureSource(options).
---
diff --git a/chrome/renderer/resources/controlled_frame/html_controlled_frame_element.js b/chrome/renderer/resources/controlled_frame/html_controlled_frame_element.js
--- a/chrome/renderer/resources/controlled_frame/html_controlled_frame_element.js
+++ b/chrome/renderer/resources/controlled_frame/html_controlled_frame_element.js
@@ -162,6 +162,23 @@
         internal.viewInstanceId, names, callback);
   }
 
+  // Experiment: returns a GuestFrameTextureSource whose read()
+  // resolves with VideoFrames backed by GPU shared images that the display
+  // compositor fills with the guest's pixels (no media capture device, no
+  // readback). `options`: width, height, maxFrameRate, poolSize, webgpu.
+  createTextureSource(options) {
+    try {
+      if (!currentGuestId(this)) {
+        return rejectedPromise(new Error('The frame has no guest'));
+      }
+      const internal = privates(this).internal;
+      return $Promise.resolve(
+          new GuestFrameTextureSource(internal.internalElement, options || {}));
+    } catch (e) {
+      return rejectedPromise(e);
+    }
+  }
+
   // Returns a Promise<MediaStream> with one video track that shows the guest's
   // contents. `options` may contain maxWidth, maxHeight, maxFrameRate (and
   // minWidth/minHeight/minFrameRate), passed through as getUserMedia legacy
